{"document_id":"industry_chassis_dwell_yard_density","chunk_id":"industry_chassis_dwell_yard_density_001","document_type":"industry_reference","terminal_id":"terminal_alpha","evidence_scope":"industry_reference","source_title":"The Impacts of Chassis Availability on Containerized Freight Flows","source_url":"https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/27806/chapter/4","publisher":"National Academies Press","published_date":"2024","subsystem":"landside","claim_type":"structural_causality","tags":["chassis","pickup_flow","import_dwell","yard_density","rehandle","qc_productivity"],"related_nodes":["chassis_availability","gate_throughput","import_dwell_time","yard_density","yard_rehandle_rate","truck_travel_time","qc_waiting","qc_productivity"],"related_edges":["chassis_availability->gate_throughput","gate_throughput->import_dwell_time","import_dwell_time->yard_density","yard_density->yard_rehandle_rate","yard_rehandle_rate->truck_travel_time","truck_travel_time->qc_waiting","qc_waiting->qc_productivity"],"scenario_ids":["qc_productivity_down_chassis_root"],"text":"Chassis shortages can reduce pickup flow, lengthen import dwell, increase yard density, create more reshuffling, and slow terminal operations. This supports explanations where QC waiting is visible but chassis-driven dwell and yard congestion are upstream."}
{"document_id":"industry_gate_delay_causes","chunk_id":"industry_gate_delay_causes_001","document_type":"industry_reference","terminal_id":"terminal_alpha","evidence_scope":"industry_reference","source_title":"Freight Performance Measurement: Travel Time in Freight-Significant Corridors","source_url":"https://ops.fhwa.dot.gov/freight/publications/eval_mc_industry/index.htm","publisher":"Federal Highway Administration","published_date":null,"subsystem":"gate","claim_type":"cause_catalog","tags":["gate","truck_wait","chassis","vessel_bunching","gate_capacity"],"related_nodes":["gate_throughput","gate_queue_length","truck_turn_time","chassis_availability","vessel_bunching","berth_occupancy"],"related_edges":["chassis_availability->gate_throughput","truck_arrival_peaking->gate_queue_length","vessel_bunching->berth_occupancy"],"scenario_ids":["truck_turn_time_up_document_root","vessel_turnaround_up_bunching_root"],"text":"Port facility delay and long truck waits can arise from gate capacity, operating-hour limits, poor chassis condition, and vessel bunching. Gate congestion may therefore be a surface symptom rather than the upstream root cause."}
{"document_id":"industry_gate_reshuffling_information","chunk_id":"industry_gate_reshuffling_information_001","document_type":"industry_reference","terminal_id":"terminal_alpha","evidence_scope":"industry_reference","source_title":"Port and Supply Chain Congestion","source_url":"https://www.congress.gov/crs_external_products/R/HTML/R44367.web.html","publisher":"Congressional Research Service","published_date":null,"subsystem":"yard","claim_type":"operational_mechanism","tags":["gate_congestion","stacking","pickup_information","reshuffling","rehandle"],"related_nodes":["gate_queue_length","yard_density","yard_rehandle_rate","truck_travel_time","truck_turn_time"],"related_edges":["yard_density->yard_rehandle_rate","yard_rehandle_rate->truck_travel_time","truck_travel_time->truck_turn_time"],"scenario_ids":["truck_turn_time_up_yard_retrieval_root"],"text":"Gate congestion can be worsened when import containers are stacked without coordinated pickup information, causing inefficient reshuffling. High truck turn time can therefore originate in yard retrieval friction rather than gate lanes."}
{"document_id":"industry_dwell_yard_utilization","chunk_id":"industry_dwell_yard_utilization_001","document_type":"industry_reference","terminal_id":"terminal_alpha","evidence_scope":"industry_reference","source_title":"Principles for Monitoring Port Performance","source_url":"https://www.haitidocs.org/doc/usaid-2018-principles-monitoring-port","publisher":"USAID","published_date":"2018","subsystem":"yard","claim_type":"structural_causality","tags":["dwell_time","yard_utilization","yard_crane_productivity","berth_productivity","gate_productivity"],"related_nodes":["import_dwell_time","yard_density","yard_crane_availability","gate_throughput","berth_productivity","truck_turn_time"],"related_edges":["import_dwell_time->yard_density","yard_density->truck_turn_time","yard_crane_availability->truck_travel_time","qc_productivity->berth_productivity"],"scenario_ids":["qc_productivity_down_yard_dwell_root","yard_density_up_warehouse_root","berth_productivity_down_yard_crane_root"],"text":"High dwell time is a common driver of high yard utilization. High yard utilization can reduce yard crane effectiveness and affect berth and gate productivity, creating structural causes behind visible quay or gate symptoms."}
{"document_id":"industry_qc_productivity_drivers","chunk_id":"industry_qc_productivity_drivers_001","document_type":"industry_reference","terminal_id":"terminal_alpha","evidence_scope":"industry_reference","source_title":"Quay Crane Productivity Influencing Factors","source_url":"https://www.mdpi.com/2077-1312/14/8/749","publisher":"MDPI","published_date":"2026","subsystem":"quay","claim_type":"cause_catalog","tags":["qc_productivity","equipment_reliability","labor","weather","terminal_congestion","yard_logistics"],"related_nodes":["qc_productivity","crane_equipment_availability","labor_availability","weather_severity","qc_waiting","yard_density","truck_travel_time"],"related_edges":["crane_equipment_availability->qc_productivity","labor_availability->qc_productivity","weather_severity->qc_productivity","truck_travel_time->qc_waiting","qc_waiting->qc_productivity"],"scenario_ids":["qc_productivity_down_yard_dwell_root","qc_productivity_down_chassis_root","qc_productivity_down_equipment_root"],"text":"QC productivity can be affected by equipment reliability, operational delays, workforce availability, weather, terminal congestion, and yard logistics. The same low QC KPI can therefore have different root causes."}
{"document_id":"industry_input_congestion","chunk_id":"industry_input_congestion_001","document_type":"industry_reference","terminal_id":"terminal_alpha","evidence_scope":"industry_reference","source_title":"Input Congestion in Port Systems","source_url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1057/s41278-025-00317-4","publisher":"Springer","published_date":"2025","subsystem":"system","claim_type":"system_dynamics","tags":["input_congestion","capacity","reinforcing_loop","resource_allocation"],"related_nodes":["berth_occupancy","yard_density","truck_travel_time","qc_waiting","qc_productivity","berth_productivity"],"related_edges":["berth_occupancy->yard_density","yard_density->truck_travel_time","truck_travel_time->qc_waiting","qc_waiting->berth_occupancy","qc_waiting->qc_productivity","qc_productivity->berth_productivity"],"scenario_ids":["vessel_turnaround_up_bunching_root","berth_productivity_down_yard_crane_root"],"text":"Input congestion describes cases where adding resources beyond the support capacity of the system can reduce output. This supports checking whether yard and transport constraints are blocking quay-side gains."}
{"document_id":"industry_yard_bottleneck_quay","chunk_id":"industry_yard_bottleneck_quay_001","document_type":"industry_reference","terminal_id":"terminal_alpha","evidence_scope":"industry_reference","source_title":"Container Terminal Yard and Quay Interaction","source_url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0191261515302599","publisher":"Transportation Research Part B","published_date":"2016","subsystem":"yard","claim_type":"bottleneck_mechanism","tags":["yard_congestion","quay_productivity","truck_interruptions","yard_layout","internal_travel_time"],"related_nodes":["yard_density","yard_rehandle_rate","yard_crane_availability","truck_travel_time","qc_waiting","qc_productivity","berth_productivity"],"related_edges":["yard_density->truck_travel_time","yard_rehandle_rate->truck_travel_time","yard_crane_availability->truck_travel_time","truck_travel_time->qc_waiting","qc_waiting->qc_productivity","qc_productivity->berth_productivity"],"scenario_ids":["qc_productivity_down_yard_dwell_root","truck_turn_time_up_yard_retrieval_root","berth_productivity_down_yard_crane_root"],"text":"Yard congestion can become the bottleneck even when quay equipment is adequate. Yard layout friction and truck interruptions can raise internal travel time, increasing QC waiting and lowering berth productivity."}
